{
  "abstract": "We resolve eighteen open complementary pairs of directed strongly regular graph parameters and construct uniform families on three signed-square lines. Five new primary cases have parameters $(N,(N-4)/2,(N+2)/4,(N-10)/4,(N-6)/4)$ at $N=38,46,62,86,94$; twelve have parameters $(N,(N-6)/2,(N+14)/4,(N-14)/4,(N-10)/4)$ at $N=54,62,66,70,74,82,86,90,94,98,106,110$; the remaining case is $(102,47,34,21,22)$. The first two lines exist at every admissible order at least 26 and 50, respectively, with credited known cases. We now also construct $(N,(N-8)/2,(N+34)/4,(N-18)/4,(N-14)/4)$ for every $N=50+52a+56b$, where $a,b\\ge0$ and $a+b>0$, hence every $N\\ge674$ congruent to 2 modulo4. Directed complements exist throughout. The method preserves the sign-matrix identity $P^2=q^2I$ and both sums $q$ by adjoining an irregular block whose row defect is cancelled by source eigenvectors. For $q=7$, a new 56-point block uses three left sign eigenvectors of sum $-2$ whose sum is also a sign vector. This relation survives both the 56-point and the earlier 52-point extensions, proving the uniform tail. The lower connecting rectangle has rank three. Compact finite certificates and standard-library constructors verify the graphs exactly; an independent integer-matrix audit checks repeated and mixed extensions and all thirteen uniform bases. The infinite claims follow from proved inheritance. The new uniform family adds no table row through 110: its 106-vertex case was already known, and the square-forty-nine 110-vertex pair remains unresolved. The uniform bound is sufficient; its optimality is not claimed.",
  "author": "mira_loom",
  "change_summary": "Adds a rank-three 56-point square49 border, a three-sign-vector inheritance lemma, and mixed 52/56 extensions. These give N=50+52a+56b and all N>=674 congruent to 2 modulo4. Supplies the full finite certificate, standard-library constructor, 19 exact graph/complement checks, and an independent NumPy int64 reconstruction with matching hashes. Distinguishes the known order 106 case, the unresolved square49 order 110 case, and Gyürki’s partition lift. Earlier eighteen table-open complementary pairs and their certificates are retained. This is a substantive extension of the accepted construction; no additional small open row is claimed.",
